From b2a48e034697179aa87e9218b9de255c19f0a0d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "erik.hauan" <erik.hauan@radiantvs.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:52:27 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] job-scheduler, schedulerwire: per-model pending ranks behind
 S2/S3

Behaviour: each scheduler NodeRank carries PendingBy (the node's pending
work split by engine/model, key PendingKey(engine, model)) and ComputedAt
(Unix ms of the compute); a recompute that only moves ComputedAt is not a new
ranking, while a PendingBy change is; Priority copies deep-clone PendingBy.

Seams used: S2 (schedulerwire.NodeRank embeds LocalRankExt, defined in
services/shared/schedulerwire/local_ext.go with PendingKey, NodeRank.Equal and
CloneRanks; Clone/Snapshot call CloneRanks and SameRanking uses
slices.EqualFunc(..., NodeRank.Equal), since the embedded map makes NodeRank
non-comparable; wire keys unchanged), S3 (schedule.go: m.localAnnotateRanks
under the state lock in rankAt, localRankUnchanged in emitIfChanged; bodies
in services/nvpair-job-scheduler/local_rank.go).

Proving tests: TestS2_Nil (shared ./schedulerwire/); TestS3_Nil,
TestLocalRankUnchangedIgnoresComputedAt, TestEmit_IncludesPendingRanksLocalExt
(nvpair-job-scheduler).

Feature-group commit for catch-up step 3, exported as
local/patches/002-scheduler-pending-by.patch. It touches only upstream files
and new files so it replays onto NVIDIA; fork-test fallout and records follow
in the fix-up commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
